## 3. Crosscheck Integration [FONT-UNIFY-CROSSCHECK]

### 3.1 Update cyd_dashboard_crosscheck.py [FONT-UNIFY-CROSSCHECK-UPDATE]

After `canvas = SkiaCanvas()`, add:

```python
atlas_path = os.path.join(_pkg_root, "composeio", "render", "font_atlas_data.json")
canvas.enable_bitmap_atlas(atlas_path)
```

All subsequent widget `draw()` calls route text through the atlas renderer.

### 3.2 Screenshot Progression [FONT-UNIFY-CROSSCHECK-SCREENSHOTS]

Save crosscheck outputs to `cyd/screenshots/progression/` with timestamp prefix:

- `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-desktop-atlas.png` — Desktop render with bitmap atlas
- `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-desktop-native.png` — Desktop render with Skia native text (for comparison)
- `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-comparison-report.txt` — pixel_comparison.py output

Also copy any CYD captures from document_store to the same directory.

---

## 4. Compliance [FONT-UNIFY-COMPLIANCE]

| ID | Requirement | Verification |
|----|-------------|-------------|
| FU-C1 | `generate_atlas.py` produces both C header and JSON from single invocation | Run generator, verify both files exist and contain same glyph count |
| FU-C2 | JSON atlas byte data matches C header byte data for every glyph | Automated comparison: parse both outputs, assert bitmap equality |
| FU-C3 | `BitmapFontAtlas.measure_text()` returns identical metrics to CYD for all test strings | Unit test with known strings at sizes 8/10/12/14/16 |
| FU-C4 | `SkiaCanvas` with bitmap atlas enabled produces text visually matching CYD | Pixel comparison: text area delta drops from 200 to < 10 |
| FU-C5 | `SkiaCanvas` without bitmap atlas works identically to current behavior | Existing 122 render engine tests pass unchanged |
| FU-C6 | Nearest-neighbor scaling in Python matches CYD integer arithmetic | Unit test: render "82C" at size 14 in Python and compare pixel-by-pixel with CYD atlas reference |
| FU-C7 | Screenshots saved to `cyd/screenshots/progression/` with timestamps | Verify files created after crosscheck run |

